# Financial Performance Dashboard

## Overview

This project presents a financial performance analysis developed in Power BI using the Global Finance & Sales Performance dataset.

The dashboard provides an overview of revenue, costs, profitability, budget performance, sales channels, product categories, and customer satisfaction.

## Dashboard Pages

### 1. Financial Overview

The first page provides a general overview of financial performance through:

- Total revenue
- Total profit
- Profit margin
- Budget performance
- Costs
- Monthly revenue and profit trends
- Revenue by region
- Revenue vs. budget by region
- Profit by product category
- Profit by region

### 2. Profitability Analysis

The second page focuses on profitability and commercial performance, including:

- Revenue by sales channel
- Profit by product category
- Average discount vs. profit margin
- Customer satisfaction by product category

## Key Insights

- Enterprise Software generated the highest profit among the analyzed product categories, while Hardware recorded the lowest.
- Partner and Online channels generated the highest revenue, while Direct sales were slightly lower.
- Customer satisfaction remained relatively consistent across product categories, with average scores around 4.2.
- Overall financial performance shows a strong relationship between revenue generation and profitability across regions and product categories.

## Tools & Technologies

- Power BI
- DAX
- Microsoft Excel
- Data Visualization
- Business Intelligence

## Dataset

The project uses the Global Finance & Sales Performance dataset.

The dataset contains financial, sales, regional, product, channel, discount, and customer satisfaction information.

